at `localhost` and at a tailnet hostname is two rows, because `WebAuthn`
makes it two credentials (docs/06-security.md#an-rp-id-is-a-domain-never-an-ip).ULID. The API-facing id -- the raw `credential_id` never leaves the
daemon in a URL.credential_idpub credential_id: Vec<u8>The raw `WebAuthn` credential id, as the authenticator issued it.pub rp_id: StringThe relying-party ID this credential is bound to, and outside which
it is worthless (docs/06-security.md#an-rp-id-is-a-domain-never-an-ip).pub credential: StringThe serialized `webauthn_rs::prelude::Passkey`: public key, signature
