e.g. a fresh `npm run build` output during development.

Unset by default, and deliberately: the old `web/dist` default was
*cwd-relative*, so it resolved under `cargo run` from the repo root
and never under launchd/systemd, where cwd is `/`. Unset means an
installed daemon is governed by the `<data_dir>/web/current` slot
(docs/18-ui-upgrades.md#the-slot) and a developer by this flag,
which is what each actually wants. Missing is not an error -- the
`npm run dev` workflow ([09](../docs/09-frontend.md#dev-workflow))
never touches this path.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 Command#Commandenum Commandrust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 Command#Service#ServiceManage this daemon's own autostart-at-login registration.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 Command#Service#action.actionaction: ServiceActionrust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 ServiceAction#ServiceActionenum ServiceActionrust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 ServiceAction#Install#InstallInstall autostart (systemd user unit; enables lingering on Linux so
it survives logout, not just re-login).rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 ServiceAction#Uninstall#UninstallRemove autostart.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 main().mainasync fn main() -> Result<()>rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 resolve_data_dir().resolve_data_dirfn resolve_data_dir(override_dir: Option<PathBuf>) -> Result<PathBuf>Resolves `<data_dir>` per docs/05-persistence.md: `--data-dir` overrides
everything; otherwise `BaseDirs::data_local_dir()/teleport`, which is
`$XDG_DATA_HOME/teleport` on Linux, `~/Library/Application Support/teleport`
on macOS, and `%LOCALAPPDATA%\teleport` on Windows — deliberately the
*local* (not roaming) dir on Windows, and with no extra path segment
`ProjectDirs` would add.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 create_data_dir().create_data_dirfn create_data_dir(dir: &Path) -> Result<()>Creates `<data_dir>` with owner-only permissions (`0700` on Unix).rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 load_or_create_token().load_or_create_tokenfn load_or_create_token(data_dir: &Path) -> Result<String>Loads `<data_dir>/token` if present, otherwise generates 256 bits from the
OS CSPRNG and writes it `0600` (docs/06-security.md#the-credential).rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 write_owner_only().write_owner_onlyfn write_owner_only(path: &Path, contents: &[u8]) -> Result<()>Writes `contents` to `path`, then (on Unix) restricts it to `0600`.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 bind_with_fallback().bind_with_fallbackasync fn bind_with_fallback(addr: SocketAddr) -> Result<TcpListener>Binds `addr`; on `EADDRINUSE` falls back to an ephemeral port on the same
IP (docs/08-packaging.md#port-discovery--do-not-hardcode-7337).rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 port_file_path().port_file_pathfn port_file_path(data_dir: &Path) -> PathBufrust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 write_port_file().write_port_filefn write_port_file(data_dir: &Path, port: u16) -> Result<()>rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 remove_port_file().remove_port_filefn remove_port_file(data_dir: &Path) -> Result<()>Removes `<data_dir>/port` on clean shutdown. Not finding it is not an
error — the file may already be gone, or never got written.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 spawn_idle_sweep_task().spawn_idle_sweep_taskfn spawn_idle_sweep_task(state: Arc<AppState>)Runs once at startup and then every 6 hours for the life of the process
(docs/05-persistence.md#garbage-collection): every `exited`/`lost` row
whose `exited_at_ms` is older than `retain_days` has its directory
deleted, then its row -- directory first, so a crash mid-GC leaves a row
with no log rather than a log with no row. Detached (`tokio::spawn`, not
awaited) -- GC is background housekeeping, not on any request path.
D3 (docs/04-api-protocol.md#get-apiv1sessions): the
only trigger for "output went quiet" is time passing with nothing
happening, so unlike every other `session_events` write this one needs a
clock, not a callback. Same shape as `spawn_gc_task` below.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 spawn_gc_task().spawn_gc_taskfn spawn_gc_task(rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 MAX_RETAIN_DAYS.MAX_RETAIN_DAYSconst MAX_RETAIN_DAYS: u64Retention is capped to ~100 years -- `retain_days as i64 * a_day_in_ms`
would otherwise wrap `i64` for a large enough `u64` config value (which
an operator setting a huge number to mean "keep forever" could plausibly
write), landing `cutoff_ms` in the *future* and making every exited/lost
row an immediate GC candidate. There is no "retain forever" setting;
the config doc should point operators at a large-but-finite number
instead.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 run_gc_pass().run_gc_passasync fn run_gc_pass(rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 url_host().url_hostfn url_host(addr: &SocketAddr) -> StringThe host to print in the startup URL. A loopback bind prints `localhost`,
not `127.0.0.1`, because **`WebAuthn` refuses an IP address as a
relying-party ID** -- a passkey cannot be enrolled or used on an
IP-literal origin, so the URL a user actually opens has to be the
`localhost` one (docs/06-security.md#an-rp-id-is-a-domain-never-an-ip).
`localhost` is equally a trustworthy origin for the secure-context rules
the rest of the SPA already depends on, so nothing else has to change.

**The bind address is untouched.** This is a display concern only; the
listener is still whatever `--listen` resolved to
(docs/06-security.md#listener).

A non-loopback bind -- the `--i-know-what-im-doing` path -- keeps its
literal address: `localhost` would resolve to the wrong machine entirely
for the remote user that flag exists to serve.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 shutdown_signal().shutdown_signalasync fn shutdown_signal(shutdown_trigger: Arc<tokio::sync::Notify>)Resolves once Ctrl+C, (Unix only) SIGTERM, or an authenticated
`POST /api/v1/shutdown` (docs/11-mvp-plan.md#m10) is received. The HTTP
trigger exists mainly for Windows, which has no SIGTERM equivalent
reachable from a console-less daemon, but is wired in on every platform
-- one uniform, curl-testable path rather than a Windows-only special
case (`api.rs`'s `shutdown` handler doc comment has the full reasoning).rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 anchor_socket_default().anchor_socket_defaultfn anchor_socket_default() -> Result<PathBuf>Where `anchord` listens when `config.toml` does not say.

Anchor's own resolution, mirrored rather than imported: teleport does not
depend on the anchor crate, so this follows its documented default of
`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/anchor.sock`, falling back to the data dir.rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 tests/rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 tests/addr().addrfn addr(ip: &str, port: u16) -> SocketAddrrust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 tests/loopback_v4_prints_localhost().loopback_v4_prints_localhostfn loopback_v4_prints_localhost()rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 tests/any_loopback_v4_address_prints_localhost().any_loopback_v4_address_prints_localhostfn any_loopback_v4_address_prints_localhost()rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 tests/loopback_v6_prints_localhost().loopback_v6_prints_localhostfn loopback_v6_prints_localhost()rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 tests/non_loopback_v4_keeps_its_literal_address().non_loopback_v4_keeps_its_literal_addressfn non_loopback_v4_keeps_its_literal_address()rust-analyzer cargo teleportd 0.1.0 tests/non_loopback_v6_is_bracketed_so_the_url_parses().non_loopback_v6_is_bracketed_so_the_url_parsesfn non_loopback_v6_is_bracketed_so_the_url_parses()installuninstallwith_env_filterwith_writerinitipis_loopbackinfolocal_addrportprintlnwith_limitswith_max_sessionswith_dblive_handlewith_graceful_shutdowndata_local_dirbindremove_fileticktick_idleflush_agent_metafrom_hourssweep_expired_auth_sessionsgc_candidatesis_ipv6ctrl_csignalrecvvar_osstd::iostd::net::{Ipv4Addr, SocketAddr}clap::{Parser, Subcommand}tokio::net::TcpListenertracing::{info, warn}teleportd::api::{build_router, AppState}teleportd::auth::{OriginPolicy, TicketStore}teleportd::log::LogLimitsteleportd::session::{SessionManager, IDLE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS, IDLE_THRESHOLD_MS}teleportd::web_assets::WebAssetsteleportd::{config, now_ms, presets}tokio::signal::unix::{signal, SignalKind}std::net::{IpAddr, Ipv6Addr}local src/main.rs 0clilet cli: Clilocal src/main.rs 1let action: ServiceActionlocal src/main.rs 2let data_dir: PathBuflocal src/main.rs 3local src/main.rs 4local src/main.rs 5let config: Configlocal src/main.rs 6let presets: Vec<Preset>local src/main.rs 7sessions_rootlet sessions