Routing by backend matters: creating in the in-process manager while the
daemon serves from anchord gives a session the API cannot see, and every
test that then attaches gets `not_found` — which looks like a protocol
bug and is really a fixture talking to the wrong store.fetch_addconst_newget_or_initfile_stemabortas_pathteleportd::api::AppStateteleportd::device::Deviceteleportd::session::{Attach, Replay, ReplayStep, SessionManager}tokio::task::JoinHandleShared test-only helpers for `daemon/tests/*.rs`.

Not a test binary itself -- cargo only auto-discovers `.rs` files
directly under `tests/` as separate integration-test crates, so a
`tests/support/mod.rs` reached via `mod support;` is invisible to that
discovery and just becomes a private module inside whichever binary
declares it. Each of those binaries gets its own copy compiled in (there
is no way to share a compiled crate between `tests/*.rs` binaries without
promoting this to a dev-dependency), but the *source* -- and the
assertions baked into it -- is written once.

Two unrelated groups of consumers share this file rather than each
getting their own: [`catch_up`] for `session_replay.rs`/
`session_catchup.rs`/`session_backpressure.rs` (drives a `Replay` to the
live boundary against an in-process `SessionManager`, no HTTP involved),
and everything below it for `http_api.rs`/`ws_protocol.rs`
(docs/10-testing.md#3-protocol-tests -- boots a real daemon on a loopback
port). Each consumer only needs some of what's here (`catch_up` never
touches HTTP; `http_api.rs` never opens a WebSocket; `ws_protocol.rs`
never inspects `base_url`), and each is compiled as its own separate test
binary -- hence the blanket `dead_code` allow rather than per-item ones.local tests/support/mod.rs 0local tests/support/mod.rs 1round_delayround_delay: Durationlocal tests/support/mod.rs 2local tests/support/mod.rs 3let mut next: u64local tests/support/mod.rs 5let mut rounds: u32local tests/support/mod.rs 6local tests/support/mod.rs 7local tests/support/mod.rs 8local tests/support/mod.rs 9local tests/support/mod.rs 11local tests/support/mod.rs 12local tests/support/mod.rs 13local tests/support/mod.rs 14local tests/support/mod.rs 15local tests/support/mod.rs 16local tests/support/mod.rs 17local tests/support/mod.rs 18local tests/support/mod.rs 19local tests/support/mod.rs 20local tests/support/mod.rs 21let n: u64local tests/support/mod.rs 22socket: &Pathlocal tests/support/mod.rs 23local tests/support/mod.rs 25local tests/support/mod.rs 26local tests/support/mod.rs 27local tests/support/mod.rs 28local tests/support/mod.rs 29local tests/support/mod.rs 30stemlet stem: Stringlocal tests/support/mod.rs 31p: PathBuflocal tests/support/mod.rs 32s: &OsStrlocal tests/support/mod.rs 33local tests/support/mod.rs 34local tests/support/mod.rs 35local tests/support/mod.rs 36let log: Filelocal tests/support/mod.rs 37local tests/support/mod.rs 38local tests/support/mod.rs 39local tests/support/mod.rs 40local tests/support/mod.rs 41local tests/support/mod.rs 42local tests/support/mod.rs 43local tests/support/mod.rs 44path_and_querypath_and_query: &strlocal tests/support/mod.rs 45local tests/support/mod.rs 46local tests/support/mod.rs 47config: Configlocal tests/support/mod.rs 49local tests/support/mod.rs 50local tests/support/mod.rs 51local tests/support/mod.rs 54local tests/support/mod.rs 55local tests/support/mod.rs 56db: Option<Db>local tests/support/mod.rs 60local tests/support/mod.rs 61web: WebAssetslocal tests/support/mod.rs 62local tests/support/mod.rs 66local tests/support/mod.rs 67local tests/support/mod.rs 68local tests/support/mod.rs 72mut config: Configlocal tests/suppor